What is Iterators?
 - Iterator is retrieve one by one element in collection objects. They are also called as cursors.
 - Type Of Iterator or cursors available in java.
   - Enumeration
   - Iterator
   - ListIterator
   - SplitIterator

 -ENUMERATION:
   - Enumeration is the first iterator that was introduced in java 1.0v It is located in java.util package.
   - It is a Legacy Interface that implements to get element one by one in legacy collection classes such as vector.
   -
   - How to create enumeration object in java?
     Enumeration is a Interface so cannot create object of enumeration directly.
     we can create object of enumeration by calling elements() of the vector class.

     public Enumeration elements()

     Enumeration e = v.elements(); // v is a vector class